1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,958
Among the three hundred replies, only a hundred described a door that failed.

2
00:00:04,958 --> 00:00:13,957
Yes, those answers also included complaints about buses, and the amount of noise in the chat was remarkable.

3
00:00:13,957 --> 00:00:34,884
“A survey is not evidence,” Professor Zhao said, “until you can characterize what it leaves out.” Three people came to the table in person: a girl from a suburban district, a waitress who worked nights, and a lass who cleaned the laboratories before dawn.

4
00:00:34,884 --> 00:00:40,779
The lady who ran the hostel and a gentleman from the alumni office sat with them.

5
00:00:40,779 --> 00:00:48,293
Mister Chen, the porter, brought a plate of ice cream, and the room began to brighten.

6
00:00:48,293 --> 00:00:51,007
Nobody altered the record.

7
00:00:51,007 --> 00:01:00,156
Whichever version they chose, the merit of the argument depended on one costly detail: the ramp had never been built.

8
00:01:00,156 --> 00:01:10,660
Supposedly it existed in a plan from 2019, and the glory of that plan lasted exactly one afternoon.

9
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:14,814
Maya kept her grasp on the practical question.

10
00:01:14,814 --> 00:01:21,963
A seedling in a cracked pot stood on the windowsill, and its odorous soil filled the small room.

11
00:01:21,963 --> 00:01:31,337
She had no talent for algebra and no interest in an empress or an ornament; she wanted a graceful sentence and a working door.

12
00:01:31,337 --> 00:01:38,546
At dusk she watched the light change and momentarily lost the thread of her own argument.

13
00:01:38,546 --> 00:01:44,355
A waitress told them that an angry customer had once tried to force the gate.

14
00:01:44,355 --> 00:01:50,554
He had told the locked door to fuck off, and the room went quiet for a moment.

15
00:01:50,554 --> 00:01:57,619
Amidst the laughter that followed, the point stood: a locked door makes people angry.

16
00:01:57,619 --> 00:02:03,783
Lest they forget it, Maya pinned the shortcoming of the old design to the wall.

17
00:02:03,783 --> 00:02:15,237
An ornamental hostess trolley, a manly poster about endurance, and a photograph of an old empire were no substitute for a ramp.

18
00:02:15,237 --> 00:02:20,731
The team agreed to familiarize themselves with the site before the next meeting.

19
00:02:20,731 --> 00:02:28,770
Maya, who often walked along the corridor after dusk, was willing to test every door herself.

20
00:02:28,770 --> 00:02:37,958
Wherever a door failed, they would mark it with a creative, suitable tag, equally visible by day and by night.

21
00:02:37,958 --> 00:02:56,421
Regarding the old plan, she said: “Good lord, we have to illustrate the failures, not merely list them.” A hilly district and a suburban one had produced completely different answers, and the saving in effort was the real discovery.

22
00:02:56,421 --> 00:03:04,205
Recently they had learned this lesson the hard way; otherwise they would still be arguing about posters.

23
00:03:04,205 --> 00:03:24,430
“Obviously,” Lin said, “we cannot depend on a plan drawn ago by people who never came here.” Plenty of folk had said the same thing for years; neither of them had listened, and the evidence was on the table, though they had yet to achieve anything.
